The attached image, Figure 6, illustrates how Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and increases antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express the highest levels of CD86, an important costimulatory molecule for T cell activation. Panel B indicates that Nano-11-adsorbed ovalbumin (OVA) is predominantly taken up by CD11b+ DCs and monocyte-derived dendritic cells (MoDCs). Panel C demonstrates that Nano-11, like aluminum hydroxide, significantly prolongs antigen retention at the injection site for several days, whereas soluble OVA clears rapidly.